From: Petr Wozniak <petr.wozniak@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] map-controller: 976 - accept AP-MLD MAC BSSID in the Client
 Association Event handler

The Topology Response associated-clients handler was already taught (v6) that
a reported BSSID may be an AP-MLD MAC that is not stored as a BSS interface,
and to track the client anyway. The Client Association Event / Topology
Notification handler was not: it does cntlr_find_fbss/bbss(ev->bssid), and on
an AP-MLD MAC both miss, so it logged "Ignore unknown STA" and returned -
dropping every dynamic MLD-client join before node_add_sta().

Mirror the sibling handler: under v6, do not drop; fall through to the
existing cntlr_add_sta/node_add_sta path (which uses ev->bssid and the node,
not fh/bh). This lets the controller's in-memory model - which steering and
map.controller status read - actually learn MLD fronthaul clients.

Signed-off-by: Petr Wozniak <petr.wozniak@gmail.com>
---
--- a/src/cntlr_map.c
+++ b/src/cntlr_map.c
@@ -221,6 +221,21 @@
 		fh = cntlr_find_fbss(c, ev->bssid);
 		bh = cntlr_find_bbss(c, ev->bssid);
 		if (!fh && !bh) {
+#if (EASYMESH_VERSION >= 6)
+			/* The reported BSSID may be the AP-MLD MAC, which is not stored
+			 * as a BSS interface. Mirror the Topology Response associated-
+			 * clients handler (already tolerant under v6): do not drop the
+			 * event; fall through and track the STA under this node with the
+			 * AP-MLD MAC as bssid (SSID stays blank until affiliated-AP
+			 * resolution is added). */
+			cntlr_dbg(LOG_STA,
+				  "%s: BSSID " MACFMT " not a BSS interface (likely AP-MLD MAC), "
+				  "accepting %sassociation event for STA " MACFMT "\n",
+				  __func__,
+				  MAC2STR(ev->bssid),
+				  associated ? "" : "dis",
+				  MAC2STR(ev->macaddr));
+#else
 			cntlr_warn(LOG_STA,
 				  "%s: Ignore unknown STA " MACFMT " %sassociation event on BSSID " MACFMT "\n",
 				  __func__,
@@ -228,6 +243,7 @@
 				  associated ? "" : "dis",
 				  MAC2STR(ev->bssid));
 			return 0;
+#endif
 		}
 
 		s = cntlr_find_sta(c->sta_table, ev->macaddr);
